course: dictionary
lesson: 5776
title: One word, several jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. The word lure can be a verb (a doing word) or a noun (a naming word). In «a falcon drops onto a swinging lure», a lure is a thing used to attract a bird, so here it is a noun.
explain: As a verb, lure means to trick or persuade someone to come somewhere, usually by offering something they want. In «a stranger offering sweets or a puppy to come with them is a known way to lure children», the sweets and the puppy are the bait, and the stranger's plan is the danger. This is why you never go with someone you do not know, and you always tell a trusted adult.
explain: Lure can also mean the pull of something, as in «the lure of the sea». That means a strong wish or attraction. All three meanings share the idea of drawing something in. When you meet a word with a new meaning, swap your idea into the sentence and see which meaning fits best.
fact: Lure can be a verb (to lure), a noun (a lure), or a noun meaning a strong pull, as in «the lure of the sea».
fact: To lure means to trick or persuade a person or animal to come somewhere, usually by offering something they want.
fact: A lure is something used to attract animals, such as fake bait that looks like a fish or insect.
fact: Safety rule: if a stranger offers sweets, a pet or a gift to make you go with them, they may be trying to lure you. Never go, and tell a trusted adult.
fact: Nature uses lures too: «A female deep-sea anglerfish has a glowing lure on her head» to draw small fish in the dark.
exercise: «A falcon drops onto a swinging lure.» In this sentence, what is a lure? | A loud noise | *Bait used to attract a bird | A person who tricks children | A bird's wing
exercise: Ella reads «a stranger offering sweets or a puppy to come with them is a known way to lure children». What does lure mean here? | To run away very fast | To give someone a present for their birthday | To make a loud noise to wake people up | *To trick someone into coming somewhere by offering something they want
exercise: Ben says, «He felt the lure of the sea every summer.» What does lure mean in this sentence? | A kind of fishing boat | *The strong pull or attraction of something | To shout loudly | A sad feeling after a holiday
test: Which sentence uses lure as a verb (a doing word)? | The fisher bought a new lure. | The lure of the sea was strong. | *The stranger tried to lure the child with sweets. | Lures are sold in the shop.
test: In «The alligator snapping turtle lures fish with a pink worm-shaped flap», what does the turtle do? | *Attracts fish to come close by offering a tempting bait | Chases fish fast across the river | Sleeps all day under a rock | Hides from the fish in the mud
exam: Someone you do not know offers you a sweet if you come with them. What is the best action? | Go with them, because they seem kind | Take the sweet and follow them to see where they live | Keep it secret and tell no one | *Say no, walk away, and tell a trusted adult
